#: ../../getting_started/guides/autoinstall_instance.rst:18
msgid ""
"Each of these constructs can be explored more deeply in their own "
"specific sections of |morpheus| docs but this guide will illustrate how "
"these pieces can be pulled together to automate deployment, ensure "
"consistency and security, and enable self-service. This could be used to "
"create a provisionable Instance Type on any |morpheus|-supported Cloud "
"type and it's intentionally left open-ended to be useful for any "
"environment. As I'm building the example, I'll show screenshots targeting"
" a build for VMware vCenter Clouds. Despite the screenshots, this guide "
"is useful for any environment."
msgstr ""
"Each of these constructs puede ser explored more deeply in their own "
"específico sections of |morpheus| docs but this guide will illustrate how "
"these pieces puede ser pulled together to automate deployment, ensure "
"consistency y security, y enable self-service. This could be used crear a "
"provisionable Instance Type on any |morpheus|-supported Cloud type y it's "
"intentionally left open-ended to be useful for any environment. As I'm "
"building the example, I'll show screenshots targeting a build for VMware "
"vCenter Clouds. Despite the screenshots, this guide is useful for any "
"environment."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/autoinstall_instance.rst:21
msgid "Create a |morpheus| Archive for Install Files"
msgstr "Create a |morpheus| Archive for Install Files"

#: ../../getting_started/guides/autoinstall_instance.rst:23
msgid ""
"|morpheus| Archives allow you to store files which can then be made "
"available for download in scripts or by users. Archives are backed by "
"buckets or file shares which must exist prior to creating the Archive. "
"Buckets could be backed by Amazon S3, for example. File Shares could be "
"backed by an NFS file share or even point directly to a local folder on "
"the appliance itself. In this example, we'll use an S3-backed bucket. "
"With an Amazon AWS Cloud already integrated with |morpheus|, we can even "
"create the S3 bucket itself without leaving |morpheus| UI."
msgstr ""
"|morpheus| Archives le permiten store files which can entonces be made "
"disponible for download in scripts o by users. Archives are backed by "
"buckets o file shares which must exist antes de creating the Archive. "
"Buckets could be backed by Amazon S3, por ejemplo. File Shares could be "
"backed by an NFS file share o even point directly to a local folder on el "
"appliance itself. In this example, we'll use an S3-backed bucket. With an "
"Amazon AWS Cloud already integrated con |morpheus|, we can even create the "
"S3 bucket itself sin leaving |morpheus| UI."

#: ../../getting_started/guides/autoinstall_instance.rst:25
msgid ""
"To create a new bucket, navigate to |InfSto|. From the Buckets tab, click"
" :guilabel:`+ ADD` and then select \"AWS S3 Bucket\". The example bucket "
"configuration is shown below. Bear in mind if you make any changes you "
"may need to carefully confirm Task configurations and calls to Cypher or "
"Archive to ensure they match any changes you've made."
msgstr ""
"To create un nuevo bucket, navigate to |InfSto|. From the Buckets tab, "
"click :guilabel:`+ ADD` y then select \\\"AWS S3 Bucket\\\". The example "
"bucket configuration is mostrado a continuación. Bear in mind if you make "
"any changes you may necesita carefully confirm Task configurations y calls "
"to Cypher o Archive to ensure they match any changes you've made."

